  "ch2-operators": {
    "id": "ch2-operators",
    "title": "Operators",
    "minutes": 3,
    "md": "#### Arithmetic operators\n\nDo maths on values and produce a new value.\n\n| Operator | Name | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `+` | Addition | adds two values |\n| `-` | Subtraction | subtracts the right from the left |\n| `*` | Multiplication | multiplies two values |\n| `/` | Division | divides the left by the right |\n| `**` | Exponentiation | raises the left to the power of the right |\n| `%` | Modulus | remainder left after division |\n| `++` | Increment | adds one to a variable |\n| `--` | Decrement | subtracts one from a variable |\n\n#### Assignment operators\n\nCompute a value and store it back in one step — shorthand for `x = x + …`.\n\n| Operator | Name | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `+=` | Add and assign | `x += 2` is `x = x + 2` |\n| `-=` | Subtract and assign | `x -= 2` is `x = x - 2` |\n| `*=` | Multiply and assign | `x *= 2` is `x = x * 2` |\n| `/=` | Divide and assign | `x /= 2` is `x = x / 2` |\n| `**=` | Exponent and assign | `x **= 2` is `x = x ** 2` |\n| `%=` | Modulus and assign | `x %= 2` is `x = x % 2` |\n\n#### Comparison operators\n\nCompare two values and return a boolean: `true` or `false`.\n\n| Operator | Name | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `==` | equal to | equal after converting types — `\"2\" == 2` is true |\n| `===` | equal to and equal type | equal value **and** type — `\"2\" === 2` is false |\n| `!=` | Loose not equal | the opposite of `==` |\n| `!==` | Strict not equal | the opposite of `===` |\n| `<` | Less than | is the left smaller? |\n| `<=` | Less than or equal | is the left smaller or the same? |\n| `>` | Greater than | is the left bigger? |\n| `>=` | Greater than or equal | is the left bigger or the same? |\n\n#### Logical operators\n\nCombine truthy / falsy values instead of comparing them.\n\n| Operator | Name | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `&&` | Logical AND | left **and** right are truthy |\n| `\\|\\|` | Logical OR | either left **or** right is truthy |\n| `??` | Nullish coalescing | right side, only when left is `null` / `undefined` |\n| `!` | Logical NOT | flips a value's truthiness |\n\n```js\nconsole.log(0 && 2); // 0\nconsole.log(1 && 2); // 2\nconsole.log(1 && 0); // 0\nconsole.log(0 || 2); // 2\nconsole.log(1 || 2); // 1\nconsole.log(0 || null); // null\nconsole.log(0 || \"\"); // \"\"\nconsole.log(false || true); // true\nconsole.log(0 || 1); // 1\nconsole.log(1 ?? \"ok\") // 1\nconsole.log(0 ?? \"ok\") // ok\nconsole.log(\"yes\" ?? \"no\") // yes\nconsole.log(\"\" ?? \"no\") // no\n```\n\nswap 2 nums\n\n```js\nlet a = 3\nlet b = 5\na = a - b\nb = a + b\na = b - a\n```\n\n```text\nor\na = a ^ b\nb = a ^ b\na= a ^ b\nconsole.log(a,b) // a=5, b=3\n```\n\nor\n\n```js\nlet a = 1\nlet b = 2\nconsole.log(a,b)\na = a + b // 1+2 =3\nb = a - b // 3-2=1\na= a - b // 3-1=2\nconsole.log(a,b)\nconsole.log(!0); // true\nconsole.log(!2); // false\n```\n\nbuildin objects\n\nMath\n\nSet\n\nDate\n\nProxy\n\nSymbol\n",
    "raw": "// # Arithmetic operators\n// +\n// -\n// *\n// /\n// **\n// %\n\n// ++\n// --\n\n\n// assignment operators\n\n// +=\n// -=\n// *=\n// /=\n// **=\n// %=\n\n\n// comparison operators\n// == equal to\n// === equal to and equal type\n// !=\n// !==\n// <\n// <=\n// >\n// >=\n\n// logical operators\n// &&\n// ||\n// ??\n// ^^\n// !\n\n// console.log(0 && 2); // 0\n// console.log(1 && 2); // 2\n// console.log(1 && 0); // 0\n\n\n// console.log(0 || 2); // 2\n// console.log(1 || 2); // 1\n// console.log(0 || null); // null\n// console.log(0 || \"\"); // \"\"\n// console.log(false || true); // true\n// console.log(0 || 1); // 1\n\n\n\n// console.log(1 ?? \"ok\") // 1\n// console.log(0 ?? \"ok\") // ok\n// console.log(\"yes\" ?? \"no\") // yes\n// console.log(\"\" ?? \"no\") // no\n\n\n// swap 2 nums\n// let a = 3\n// let b = 5\n\n// a = a - b\n// b = a + b\n// a = b - a \n\n// //or\n\n// a = a ^ b\n// b = a ^ b\n// a= a ^ b\n\n// console.log(a,b) // a=5, b=3\n\n// or\n\n// let a = 1\n// let b = 2\n// console.log(a,b)\n\n// a = a + b // 1+2 =3\n// b = a - b // 3-2=1\n// a= a - b // 3-1=2\n\n// console.log(a,b)\n\n// console.log(!0); // true\n// console.log(!2); // false\n\n\n// buildin objects\n// Math\n// Set\n// Date\n// Proxy\n// Symbol"
  },
