    "title": "Loops",
    "minutes": 3,
    "md": "while statement\n\n```js\nvar i = 1\nwhile(i<=5){\n    console.log(i);\n    i++\n}\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n```\n\ndo while\n\n```js\nlet i = 1\ndo{\n    console.log(i);\n    i++\n}while(i<=3)\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n1\n2\n3\n```\n\nfor loop\n\n```js\nfor(let i=1; i<=3; i++){\n    console.log(i);\n}\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n1\n2\n3\n```\n\n```js\nfor(let i=1; i<=5; i++){\n    if(i==3){\n        break\n    }\n    console.log(i); // 1 2\n}\nfor(let i=1; i<=3; i++){\n    if(i==2){\n        continue\n    }\n    console.log(i); // 1 3\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n- **for..in** — loop\n\nfor...in loop iterates over obj `name / property`\n\n#### Syntax\n\n```js\nfor(var in obj) {\n```\n\nexe code\n\n```js\n}\n```\n\n#### Ex1\n\n```js\nlet obj = {\n```\n\nname: 'art',\n\nage: 21,\n\ncity: 'Mumbai'\n\n```js\n}\nfor(props in obj) {\n    console.log(props,\": \", obj[props])\n}\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\nname: art\nage: 21\ncity: Mumbai\n```\n\n---\n\nex2: Array\n\n```js\nlet arr = []\narr.name = 'art'\narr.age = 21\narr.city = 'Mumbai'\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n\"name\" \"art\"\n\"age\" 21\n\"city\" \"Mumbai\"\n```\n\n```js\nfor(let props in arr) {\n    console.log(props, arr[props])\n}\nlet arr = [1,2,3,4]\nfor(let props in arr) {\n    console.log(props, arr[props])\n}\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n\"0\" 1\n\"1\" 2\n\"2\" 3\n\"3\" 4\n```\n\n---\n\nProblem of for..in loop with Array:\n\n```js\nconst fruits = ['apple', 'banana', 'orange'];\n```\n\n❌ DON'T use for...in with arrays\n\n```js\nfor (const index in fruits) {\n  console.log(fruits[index]); // 'apple', 'banana', 'orange'\n}\n```\n\nSeems `fine? But` watch what happens when we add a custom property:\n\n```js\nArray.prototype.customMethod = function() { return 'custom'; };\nfruits.customProperty = 'I am a custom property';\n```\n\nNow for...in behaves unexpectedly:\n\n```js\nfor (const index in fruits) {\n  console.log(index, fruits[index]);\n}\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n0 apple\n1 banana\n2 orange\ncustomProperty I am a custom property  ← Unexpected!\ncustomMethod function() { return 'custom'; } ← Unexpected!\n```\n\n---\n\nfor..of loop\n\nfor...of loop iterates over obj value\n\n```js\nnote: does not works on obj {}, only array\n```\n\n#### Example\n\n```js\nlet obj = {\n\tname: \"art\",\n\tage: 21\n}\nfor(let i of obj) {\n\tconsole.log(i)\n}\n```\n\ngives error: TypeError: obj is not iterable\n\n#### Ex1\n\n```js\nconst arr = [3, 5, 7];\narr.foo = \"hello\";\nfor (const i in arr) {\n  console.log(i);\n}\n```\n\n```text\n\"0\" \"1\" \"2\" \"foo\"\n```\n\n```js\nfor (const i of arr) {\n  console.log(i);\n}\n```\n\n```text\n3 5 7\n```\n\n---\n\n#### Ex2\n\n```js\nconst obj = { foo: 1, bar: 2 };\nfor (const [key, val] of Object.entries(obj)) { // used Object.entries() cuz it returns arr -> [['foo',1], ['bar',2]]\n  console.log(key, val);\n}\n```\n\n```text\n\"foo\" 1\n\"bar\" 2\n```\n",
