  "ch4-destructuring": {
    "id": "ch4-destructuring",
    "title": "Destructuring",
    "minutes": 3,
    "md": "array\n\n```js\nlet arr = [1,2,3]\nconst [a,b,c] = arr\nconsole.log(a,b,c) // 1 2 3\nconst [e,,f] = arr\nconsole.log(e,f) // 1 3\n```\n\narr and func\n\n```js\nfunction a() {\n    return [1,2]\n}\nlet [x,y] = a()\nconsole.log(x,y) // 1 2\n```\n\nswap values\n\n```js\nlet a= 1\nlet b =2; // need to add semi-colon\n[a,b] = [b,a]\nconsole.log(a,b) // 2 1\n```\n\nobj\n\n```js\nconst obj = {\n    name :\"ok\",\n    age: 12,\n    country: \"INDIA\"\n}\nconst {name, age} = obj\nconsole.log(name, age) // \"ok\" 12\n```\n\n```text\nfunction parameters destructuring\n```\n\n```js\nlet arr = [1,2,3]\nfunction fn(a,b,c) {\n\tconsole.log(a,b,c)\n}\nfn(arr) // [1,2,3] undefined undefined\nfunction fn1([a,b,c]) {\n\tconsole.log(a,b,c)\n}\nfn1(arr) // 1 2 3\n```\n\n---\n\n```js\nlet obj = {\n\tname: \"Art\",\n\tage: 21\n}\nfunction fn({name: x, age: y}) {\n\tconsole.log(x, y)\n}\nfn(obj) // Art 21\n```\n",
    "raw": "// array\nlet arr = [1,2,3]\nconst [a,b,c] = arr\nconsole.log(a,b,c) // 1 2 3\n\nconst [e,,f] = arr\nconsole.log(e,f) // 1 3\n\n\n\n// arr and func\nfunction a() {\n    return [1,2]\n}\nlet [x,y] = a()\nconsole.log(x,y) // 1 2\n\n\n// swap values\n// let a= 1\n// let b =2; // need to add semi-colon\n\n// [a,b] = [b,a]\n// console.log(a,b) // 2 1\n\n\n//obj\nconst obj = {\n    name :\"ok\",\n    age: 12,\n    country: \"INDIA\"\n}\nconst {name, age} = obj\nconsole.log(name, age) // \"ok\" 12\n\n\n\n\n// // function parameters destructuring\n// let arr = [1,2,3]\n\n// function fn(a,b,c) {\n// \tconsole.log(a,b,c) \n// }\n// fn(arr) // [1,2,3] undefined undefined\n\n\n// function fn1([a,b,c]) {\n// \tconsole.log(a,b,c)\n// }\n// fn1(arr) // 1 2 3\n\n\n\n// ---------------\n// let obj = {\n// \tname: \"Art\",\n// \tage: 21\n// }\n\n// function fn({name: x, age: y}) {\n// \tconsole.log(x, y)\n// }\n\n// fn(obj) // Art 21"
  },
  "ch4-hoisting": {
    "id": "ch4-hoisting",
    "title": "Hoisting",
    "minutes": 3,
    "md": "```js\nconsole.log(a) // undefined\nvar a = 1\n```\n\nsame as\n\n```js\nvar a  // puts the var declaration to the top\nconsole.log(a)\na = 1\n```\n\nfunctions are hoisted over variable\n\n```js\nconsole.log(a) // function a() {}\nvar a = 1\nfunction a() {\n  console.log(\"ok\")\n}\n```\n\nHoisting: It is a process done by the JS runtime engine during the compilation phase,\n\nwhere it scans the entire js code for declarations\n\nsuch as: var, let, const, function and class.\n\nwhen in exection phase the js engine see the code\n\nconsider this code\n\n```js\nconsole.log(a) // undefined, cuz in compilation phase the JIT compiler has stored the var a in RAM and intialzed it with undefined\nvar a = 1\n```\n\nHoisting works differently for let, const, and classes apart from var and fns.\n",
    "raw": "// console.log(a) // undefined\n// var a = 1\n\n\n// same as\n// var a  // puts the var declaration to the top\n// console.log(a)\n// a = 1\n\n\n// functions are hoisted over variable\n// console.log(a) // function a() {}\n// var a = 1\n// function a() {\n//   console.log(\"ok\")\n// }\n\n\n\n// Hoisting: It is a process done by the JS runtime engine during the compilation phase,\n//  where it scans the entire js code for declarations \n// such as: var, let, const, function and class.\n\n// when in exection phase the js engine see the code\n// consider this code\nconsole.log(a) // undefined, cuz in compilation phase the JIT compiler has stored the var a in RAM and intialzed it with undefined\nvar a = 1\n\n\n\n// Hoisting works differently for let, const, and classes apart from var and fns."
  },
